.TH KBDTYPE 8
.SH NAME
kbdtype \- type into the keyboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aux/kbdtype
.I text
.br
.B aux/kbdtype
.B -p
|
.B -r
.I hex
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Kbdtype
writes keyboard messages to
.BR /dev/kbdin ,
as if they had been typed
.RI ( kbdfs (8)):
each rune of
.I text
as a
.B c
message, each with its null byte, which
.IR echo (1)
cannot write.
With
.B -p
or
.BR -r ,
the key of the rune
.I hex
(hexadecimal, as
.B f868
for Kmod4) is pressed or let go: an
.B r
or
.B R
message, of which kbdfs makes the
.BR k ,
.B K
and
.B c
messages a program reads.
It is for tests and scripts that drive a window system, as sys/src/build/host/tests/ui's and
sys/src/build/host/tests/gpu's do.
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/cmd/aux/kbdtype.c
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR kbdfs (8),
.IR keyboard (6),
.IR wsys (4)
.SH HISTORY
9space's.
